From: mscharged-port
Subject: Tweak: a fast replay's effects age with the match
Upstream-base: 8b9d92dd88b4c727cc6359ee4cd5ba128cced7b8

The particle effects age once a drawn frame (ParticleUpdateTask::Run), by
the frame's time; a match takes about one step in that time. A replay that
plays faster takes several steps a frame (twice or four times as fast, or a
live replay catching up, tweak patches 0071 and 0086), and its steps start
effects faster than the frames end them. Catching up they piled up by the
hundreds, and the game's instant-replay recorder, which keeps every effect
in each frame it records (EmissionManager::Replay), outgrew the 32 KB its
frames have (Replay::Record does not check): it wrote over the frames after
it and beyond its memory, and the replay crashed (live spectators, most
often with a texture pack, whose slower frames take more steps).

While a replay plays faster than its match, the effects now age by the
match's time (mscharged_tweak_replay_effects_time): the time of the steps
taken since the last update while it catches up, the frame's time times its
speed otherwise; in updates of at most 0.1 s. A match, and a replay at its
own pace, age them as before.

diff --git a/include/mscharged_replay.h b/include/mscharged_replay.h
--- a/include/mscharged_replay.h
+++ b/include/mscharged_replay.h
@@ -55,6 +55,9 @@
 // How many times faster the wipes around cutscenes run: more than 1 while a
 // live replay catches up.
 float mscharged_tweak_replay_wipe_speed(void);
+// The time the effects age in a frame whose update took `dt` (tweak patch
+// 0089): `dt` for a match, the match's time for a replay faster than it.
+float mscharged_tweak_replay_effects_time(float dt);
 // The title (passed as by Skip intro): whether it starts the replay's match
 // instead of going to the main menu, once; then, from its update, the start.
 bool mscharged_tweak_take_replay_start(void);
diff --git a/src/Game/Task/ParticleUpdateTask.cpp b/src/Game/Task/ParticleUpdateTask.cpp
--- a/src/Game/Task/ParticleUpdateTask.cpp
+++ b/src/Game/Task/ParticleUpdateTask.cpp
@@ -6,6 +6,9 @@
 #if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
 #include "mscharged_rollback.h"
 #endif
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+#include "mscharged_replay.h"
+#endif
 
 ParticleUpdateTask* ParticleUpdateTask::sInstance;
 
@@ -47,7 +50,20 @@
     if (mUpdateEnabled && update)
     {
         EmissionManager* manager = EmissionManager::Instance();
+#if defined(MSCHARGED_TWEAKS)
+        // A replay faster than its match takes several steps a frame, and
+        // they start effects faster than a frame's time ends them: they age
+        // by the match's time then, in updates of at most 0.1 s.
+        float age = mscharged_tweak_replay_effects_time(dt * mTimeScale);
+        while (age > 0.1f)
+        {
+            manager->Update(0.1f);
+            age -= 0.1f;
+        }
+        manager->Update(age);
+#else
         manager->Update(dt * mTimeScale);
+#endif
     }
 
     bool render = true;
